The competitive starting point was the category's familiar emphasis on **softness and price**. In the deck, the team developed an alternative direction around care shown through small, everyday actions in Vietnamese families.

The insight slide frames a tension: these acts of care can be easy to overlook, including for the person doing them. The proposed positioning connects the caregiver's daily attention with the everyday role of the product. This is the team's planning interpretation, rather than a claim that every family behaves the same way.

I helped develop the reasoning and copy, including **“Nâng niu yêu thương mỗi ngày, từ những điều nhỏ bé nhất.”** The slides below show how that route became a proposed strategic approach and message platform.
